   Cross-multiplication of key features might amplify the interactions between chemical properties. For example:
   - C% represents the percentage of carbon atoms, while SpMax_A is an eigenvalue feature related to the adjacency matrix. Their product may highlight the relationship between carbon density and molecular topology.
   - The product of SpPosA_B(p) (polarizability measure) and Me (mean electronegativity) may represent global polarizability interacting with the atom's electronegativity.

   
