   <Electronegativity_Polarizability_Interaction><multiply><Me><SpPosA_B(p)><Product_of_mean_electronegativity_and_polarizability_indicating_global_interactions>
   

3. Adding ratio features to highlight molecular proportions.
   Ratios can emphasize relative interactions between certain categories. Features such as the number of oxygen atoms (nO) with respect to the total carbon density (C%), or halogen atoms (nX) as a proportion of total heavy atoms (nHM), can be meaningful. These features may represent key molecular proportion effects.

   
